* EPC2067 typical scalar parameters - official EPC datasheet, revised 2021-10-21
* EXTERNAL_DEVICE_DATA, not values printed in P24/P25 text.
* This is the device 2024 Table 3 names for the nP=4 embedded/GaN-package
* row (2 parallel high-side, 3 parallel low-side for nM=4); it is NOT the
* device the present active P25_SUPPLEMENT commutation branch uses.
* Conditions/meaning must remain attached to each value.
.param EPC2067_VRATED=40
.param EPC2067_RDS_TYP_25C=1.55m
.param EPC2067_COSS_TYP=1607p
.param EPC2067_COER_0_20V=1597p
.param EPC2067_COTR_0_20V=1860p
.param EPC2067_QOSS_20V=56n
* COTR is specified for a 0-to-20-V transition (0 to 50% of the 40 V BVDSS),
* not 0-to-48-V or 0-to-50-V like the GS61008T sheet's COTR. Any use across a
* different voltage swing than 0-20 V is an extrapolation unless the
* nonlinear Coss/Qoss curve is implemented.
* BVDSS=40 V continuous (48 V pulsed) is below the full 48 V bus; this is
* only plausible because each switch in the flying-capacitor ladder is
* expected to block roughly Vin/nP (~12 V for nP=4), not the full 48 V --
* this has not been independently confirmed against the netlist's actual
* per-switch blocking voltage and must be checked before this device is
* used in any active branch.
